This file is the next git commit message (`git commit -F`). Keep it cumulative.

Agents: **append** a short why after each slice of work. Do not replace the
whole file with only the latest turn.

After commit.sh succeeds, the file becomes `committed <timestamp>`. The next
WIP should replace that stamp (or write below it).

Example:
Land fleet SSH so Cursor keeps one Host thin_host while LAN/ZT is only TCP.
